  "label": "The speaker is mapped onto the Black man in the image",
  "description": "The text 'the day i realized i didn't need no bitch to bust a nut' is spoken by the man depicted in the image. The visual material (the man) is the entity being mapped onto by the textual material, as the text is presented as a personal revelation or statement from the man shown. The man's expressive face and gesturing hands reinforce the idea that he is the one speaking the text, making this a direct analogical mapping where the visual entity represents the speaker of the text.",
